    "rtf_explanation": "Real-Time Factor (RTF = execution time / audio duration) measures computational throughput, not latency. A raw ONNX model with RTF = 0.0087 (26ms / 3000ms) can process audio 115x faster than real time. However, acoustic event detection fundamentally requires accumulating audio in physical time to form the 3.0-second frequency resolution window. Therefore, physical accumulation latency is bounded below by (3.0s - onset_time), making instantaneous (zero-latency) bioacoustic classification physically impossible regardless of compute speed."
